{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.12.13","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"competition","sourceId":143678}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Solar Filament Segmentation Challenge 2026 - YOLO26 Full-Resolution Baseline\n\nThis notebook trains and evaluates a YOLO26 segmentation model on the original 2048 x 2048 images while staying within a 30 GiB RAM and 57.6 GiB disk budget.\n\n## Resource settings\n\n- **2048 x 2048 input resolution** for training, validation, and test inference.\n- **Both available T4 GPUs** for training, with a global batch of 2 (one image per GPU).\n- **At most four CPU data workers** during training (two per GPU); CPU preprocessing pools also use at most four single-threaded workers.\n- **Adaptive disk cache**: use it only when the actual working volume can fit it with headroom; otherwise disable caching. RAM caching is never used.\n- **One image per inference batch** and a bounded validation queue to keep full-resolution masks from accumulating.\n- Submission CSV validation reads rows incrementally rather than loading all RLE strings into RAM.\n\nValidation metrics include PQ, SQ, RQ, Dice, IoU, precision, recall, and instance error counts. Test ground truth is never accessed.","metadata":{"_uuid":"f6664c60-bfd0-4fb7-97ef-b6f3b733e1e6","_cell_guid":"1b838603-0ce3-49c1-b028-ffe3ff3818f0","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Install dependencies and import libraries\n\nThe training configuration uses disk caching rather than a RAM cache. Package installation disables pip's wheel cache to conserve the session disk.","metadata":{"_uuid":"45dba8dc-0f2b-4eed-bb41-b745a3b59295","_cell_guid":"e9e20865-7d45-4de7-93eb-28cdb337c6cb","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"%pip install -q --no-cache-dir -U ultralytics pycocotools scikit-learn pandas matplotlib tqdm torchmetrics threadpoolctl psutil","metadata":{"_uuid":"c114cc6d-4515-4016-8d35-c8231f8830a7","_cell_guid":"1d6398ae-5847-4f6d-9276-a196d6589f84","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-01T08:47:13.011648Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-01T08:47:13.012403Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-01T08:47:18.890697Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-01T08:47:13.012369Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-01T08:47:18.889653Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from pathlib import Path\nimport os\nimport csv\nimport gc\nimport random\nimport shutil\nimport time\nimport warnings\nimport multiprocessing\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom functools import partial\n\nimport cv2\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport torch\ntry:\n    import psutil\nexcept ImportError:\n    psutil = None\n\nfrom pycocotools import mask as mask_utils\nfrom pycocotools.coco import COCO\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import GroupShuffleSplit\nfrom tqdm.auto import tqdm\nfrom torchmetrics.segmentation import DiceScore\nfrom threadpoolctl import threadpool_limits\nfrom ultralytics import YOLO\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=UserWarning)\n\nDEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\nCUDA_DEVICE_COUNT = torch.cuda.device_count() if torch.cuda.is_available() else 0\nMAX_GPUS_TO_USE = 2\nGPU_DEVICE_IDS = list(range(min(CUDA_DEVICE_COUNT, MAX_GPUS_TO_USE)))\nGPU_COUNT_USED = len(GPU_DEVICE_IDS)\n\nif GPU_COUNT_USED >= 2:\n    TRAIN_DEVICE = GPU_DEVICE_IDS\nelif GPU_COUNT_USED == 1:\n    TRAIN_DEVICE = GPU_DEVICE_IDS[0]\nelse:\n    TRAIN_DEVICE = \"cpu\"\n\n# Ultralytics prediction uses one explicit device; distributed training below\n# uses both GPUs when they are available.\nINFERENCE_DEVICE = GPU_DEVICE_IDS[0] if GPU_COUNT_USED else \"cpu\"\n\nprint(f\"Training device(s): {TRAIN_DEVICE}\")\nprint(f\"Inference device: {INFERENCE_DEVICE}\")\nif CUDA_DEVICE_COUNT:\n    for gpu_id in GPU_DEVICE_IDS:\n        print(f\"GPU {gpu_id}: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(gpu_id)}\")\n    print(f\"CUDA devices available: {CUDA_DEVICE_COUNT}; using {GPU_COUNT_USED}\")\n\nCPU_COUNT = os.cpu_count() or 1\nprint(f\"Logical CPU count: {CPU_COUNT}\")","metadata":{"_uuid":"f1ac1b7d-fcf9-43f6-8f24-255a97ab728f","_cell_guid":"0be8d229-8b61-43ea-bce8-97579d8ad990","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-02T15:07:36.52701Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-02T15:07:36.527258Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-02T15:07:36.954383Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-02T15:07:36.52723Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-02T15:07:36.953477Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Creating new Ultralytics Settings v0.0.8 file ✅ \nView Ultralytics Settings with 'yolo settings' or at '/root/.config/Ultralytics/settings.json'\nUpdate Settings with 'yolo settings key=value', i.e. 'yolo settings runs_dir=path/to/dir'. For help see https://docs.ultralytics.com/usage/settings.\nTraining device(s): [0, 1]\nInference device: 0\nGPU 0: Tesla T4\nGPU 1: Tesla T4\nCUDA devices available: 2; using 2\nLogical CPU count: 4\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Configure paths and experiment\n\nThe notebook caps CPU worker processes at four. Multi-GPU training uses two data workers per GPU (four total); custom preprocessing stages use a four-process pool with one thread per worker. Images and inference masks remain at 2048 x 2048, while batches and queues stay small to protect the 30 GiB RAM limit.","metadata":{"_uuid":"0b0612ce-4b86-4462-a923-bcd7344a1037","_cell_guid":"7204f771-3b2e-44e5-bf0f-8c339cdca5b2","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"SEED = 42\n\nNUM_EPOCHS = 1\n\nVALIDATION_FRACTION = 0.20\nPATIENCE = 10\n\nIMAGE_SIZE = 2048\nNUM_WORKERS = 4  # Hard cap for custom CPU worker pools.\nWORKER_CPU_THREADS = 1\n\n# In Ultralytics DDP, workers is per GPU rank. Keep the global worker count <= 4.\nYOLO_WORKERS_PER_GPU = (\n    min(NUM_WORKERS // GPU_COUNT_USED, 4)\n    if GPU_COUNT_USED > 0\n    else 0\n)\nBATCH_SIZE = GPU_COUNT_USED if GPU_COUNT_USED > 0 else 1  # One image per GPU.\n\n# One native-resolution image at a time keeps full-size masks bounded.\nVAL_BATCH_SIZE = 1\nMAX_PENDING_VALIDATION = NUM_WORKERS * 2\nMAX_DETECTIONS = 100\n\nRAM_LIMIT_GIB = 30.0\nRAM_RESERVE_GIB = 6.0\nDISK_LIMIT_GIB = 57.6\nDISK_RESERVE_GIB = 10.0  # Preferred reserve; reduced only if the mounted volume requires it.\nMIN_DISK_RESERVE_GIB = 4.0\nCACHE_SAFETY_FACTOR = 1.25\nTRAIN_OUTPUT_RESERVE_GIB = 2.0\nGIB = 1024 ** 3\nYOLO_CACHE_MODE = \"disk\"  # Preflight switches this to False if disk cache cannot fit.\nACTIVE_DISK_RESERVE_GIB = DISK_RESERVE_GIB\n\nMIN_COMPONENT_AREA = 20\nYOLO_MODEL_NAME = \"yolo26s-seg.pt\"\n\nYOLO_DATA_DIR = Path.cwd() / \"yolo_filament_dataset\"\nRUNS_DIR = Path.cwd() / \"yolo_runs\"\nRUN_NAME = \"yolo26s_filament_full_resolution\"\nDATA_YAML = YOLO_DATA_DIR / \"filament.yaml\"\n\nSUBMISSION_PATH = Path.cwd() / \"solar_filament_yolo26s_submission.csv\"\nFINAL_METRICS_PATH = Path.cwd() / \"solar_filament_yolo26s_validation_metrics.csv\"\nPER_IMAGE_METRICS_PATH = Path.cwd() / \"solar_filament_yolo26s_per_image_metrics.csv\"\n\nREBUILD_YOLO_DATASET = True\nCREATE_SUBMISSION = True\n\nCONFIDENCE_CANDIDATES = (0.15, 0.25, 0.35, 0.45, 0.55)\nPQ_MATCH_IOU = 0.50\n\n\ndef _read_cgroup_memory_pair(limit_path, current_path):\n    try:\n        limit_text = Path(limit_path).read_text().strip()\n        current_text = Path(current_path).read_text().strip()\n        if limit_text == \"max\":\n            return None\n        limit_bytes = int(limit_text)\n        current_bytes = int(current_text)\n        if limit_bytes >= (1 << 60):  # cgroup v1 unlimited sentinel\n            return None\n        return max(0, limit_bytes - current_bytes)\n    except (OSError, ValueError):\n        return None\n\n\ndef available_ram_bytes():\n    for limit_path, current_path in (\n        (\"/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.max\", \"/sys/fs/cgroup/memory.current\"),\n        (\"/sys/fs/cgroup/memory/memory.limit_in_bytes\", \"/sys/fs/cgroup/memory/memory.usage_in_bytes\"),\n    ):\n        available = _read_cgroup_memory_pair(limit_path, current_path)\n        if available is not None:\n            return available\n    if psutil is not None:\n        try:\n            return int(psutil.virtual_memory().available)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    return None\n\n\ndef require_ram_headroom(stage, minimum_gib):\n    available = available_ram_bytes()\n    if available is None:\n        print(f\"[RAM] Could not read a runtime memory limit before {stage}; using bounded batches/workers.\")\n        return\n    available_gib = available / GIB\n    print(f\"[RAM] Available before {stage}: {available_gib:.1f} GiB\")\n    if available_gib < minimum_gib:\n        raise MemoryError(\n            f\"Only {available_gib:.1f} GiB RAM is available before {stage}; \"\n            f\"need at least {minimum_gib:.1f} GiB to preserve headroom under the \"\n            f\"{RAM_LIMIT_GIB:.1f} GiB session limit. Free memory or restart the session.\"\n        )\n\n\ndef directory_size_bytes(root):\n    root = Path(root)\n    if not root.exists():\n        return 0\n    total = 0\n    for item in root.rglob(\"*\"):\n        if item.is_file() and not item.is_symlink():\n            try:\n                total += item.stat().st_size\n            except OSError:\n                pass\n    return total\n\n\ndef preflight_training_resources(train_split, val_split, image_dir):\n    global YOLO_CACHE_MODE, ACTIVE_DISK_RESERVE_GIB\n\n    require_ram_headroom(\"dataset preparation\", minimum_gib=RAM_RESERVE_GIB + 2.0)\n    records = pd.concat([train_split, val_split], ignore_index=True)\n\n    # Conservative cache estimate: RGB uint8 array per YOLO record at full size.\n    estimated_cache_bytes = int(\n        len(records) * IMAGE_SIZE * IMAGE_SIZE * 3 * CACHE_SAFETY_FACTOR\n    )\n    # Copies are only used if symlink creation is unavailable; count duplicate records too.\n    copy_bytes = 0\n    for file_name in records[\"file_name\"]:\n        source = Path(image_dir) / file_name\n        if source.is_file():\n            copy_bytes += source.stat().st_size\n\n    output_reserve = int(TRAIN_OUTPUT_RESERVE_GIB * GIB)\n    workspace_bytes = directory_size_bytes(Path.cwd())\n    disk = shutil.disk_usage(YOLO_DATA_DIR.parent)\n    effective_budget_bytes = min(int(DISK_LIMIT_GIB * GIB), int(disk.total))\n\n    # Prefer disk caching with the full reserve. If the mounted filesystem is\n    # smaller than the advertised session quota, turn caching off (never RAM-on)\n    # and only reduce the reserve as far as 4 GiB.\n    cache_options = ((\"disk\", estimated_cache_bytes), (False, 0))\n    reserve_options = [\n        value for value in (DISK_RESERVE_GIB, 8.0, 6.0, MIN_DISK_RESERVE_GIB)\n        if value <= DISK_RESERVE_GIB\n    ]\n    selected_plan = None\n\n    for cache_mode, cache_bytes in cache_options:\n        for reserve_gib in reserve_options:\n            reserve_bytes = int(reserve_gib * GIB)\n            planned_new_bytes = cache_bytes + copy_bytes + output_reserve + reserve_bytes\n            if (\n                planned_new_bytes <= effective_budget_bytes\n                and workspace_bytes + planned_new_bytes <= effective_budget_bytes\n                and disk.free >= planned_new_bytes\n            ):\n                selected_plan = (cache_mode, reserve_gib, planned_new_bytes, cache_bytes)\n                break\n        if selected_plan is not None:\n            break\n\n    if selected_plan is None:\n        no_cache_minimum = (\n            copy_bytes\n            + output_reserve\n            + int(MIN_DISK_RESERVE_GIB * GIB)\n        )\n        raise OSError(\n            \"Insufficient writable disk even with YOLO image caching disabled. \"\n            f\"Filesystem capacity: {disk.total / GIB:.1f} GiB; free: {disk.free / GIB:.1f} GiB; \"\n            f\"workspace: {workspace_bytes / GIB:.1f} GiB; minimum planned use: \"\n            f\"{no_cache_minimum / GIB:.1f} GiB (includes a {MIN_DISK_RESERVE_GIB:.1f} GiB reserve). \"\n            \"Free disk space or select a larger working volume.\"\n        )\n\n    YOLO_CACHE_MODE, ACTIVE_DISK_RESERVE_GIB, planned_new_bytes, cache_bytes = selected_plan\n    print(\n        f\"[DISK] Cache mode: {YOLO_CACHE_MODE}; estimated cache: {cache_bytes / GIB:.1f} GiB; \"\n        f\"worst-case image copies: {copy_bytes / GIB:.2f} GiB.\"\n    )\n    print(\n        f\"[DISK] Planned additional use: {planned_new_bytes / GIB:.1f} GiB; \"\n        f\"reserved free space: {ACTIVE_DISK_RESERVE_GIB:.1f} GiB; \"\n        f\"filesystem free: {disk.free / GIB:.1f} GiB.\"\n    )\n    if YOLO_CACHE_MODE is False:\n        print(\"[DISK] Full-resolution training will continue without image caching; RAM caching is disabled.\")\n\n\ndef set_seed(seed=SEED):\n    random.seed(seed)\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    torch.manual_seed(seed)\n    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n        torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(seed)\n\n\ndef configure_main_process_threads():\n    cv2.setNumThreads(WORKER_CPU_THREADS)\n    try:\n        torch.set_num_threads(WORKER_CPU_THREADS)\n    except RuntimeError:\n        pass\n\n\nconfigure_main_process_threads()\nset_seed()\n\n# --- Logging Framework Configurations ---\nprint(f\"Random seed initialization: {SEED}\")\nprint(f\"Split ratio: Train = {1.0 - VALIDATION_FRACTION:.2f} / Validation = {VALIDATION_FRACTION:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Training epochs: {NUM_EPOCHS} (Early stopping patience: {PATIENCE})\")\nprint(f\"Input size: {IMAGE_SIZE} x {IMAGE_SIZE}\")\nprint(f\"Custom CPU worker cap: {NUM_WORKERS}\")\nprint(f\"YOLO data workers per GPU: {YOLO_WORKERS_PER_GPU}\")\nprint(f\"YOLO global batch size: {BATCH_SIZE}\")\nprint(f\"Inference batch size: {VAL_BATCH_SIZE}\")\nprint(\"Image cache mode: selected by disk preflight; RAM caching is disabled.\")","metadata":{"_uuid":"1677721e-44e9-4a1b-975b-93819e56e1d7","_cell_guid":"781a4db4-f281-41e6-88b5-5bdde6c22e7c","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-02T15:07:55.846284Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-02T15:07:55.847018Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-02T15:07:55.900256Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-02T15:07:55.846978Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-02T15:07:55.89938Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Random seed initialization: 42\nSplit ratio: Train = 0.80 / Validation = 0.20\nTraining epochs: 1 (Early stopping patience: 10)\nInput size: 2048 x 2048\nCustom CPU worker cap: 4\nYOLO data workers per GPU: 2\nYOLO global batch size: 2\nInference batch size: 1\nImage cache mode: selected by disk preflight; RAM caching is disabled.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def find_dataset_root():\n    expected = \"MAGFiLO_1.0_Annotations_kaggle2026_train.json\"\n\n    candidates = [\n        Path.cwd(),\n        Path.cwd().parent,\n        Path(\"/kaggle/input\"),\n    ]\n\n    for parent in candidates:\n        if not parent.exists():\n            continue\n\n        for annotation in parent.glob(\n            \"**/\" + expected\n        ):\n            root = annotation.parent.parent\n\n            if (\n                (\n                    root\n                    / \"train\"\n                    / \"train_images\"\n                ).is_dir()\n                and (\n                    root\n                    / \"test\"\n                    / \"test_images\"\n                ).is_dir()\n            ):\n                return root\n\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\n        \"Could not find MAGFiLO_1.0_Kaggle_2026 \"\n        \"with train and test image folders.\"\n    )\n\n\nDATA_ROOT = find_dataset_root()\n\nTRAIN_DIR = DATA_ROOT / \"train\"\nTRAIN_IMAGE_DIR = TRAIN_DIR / \"train_images\"\nTEST_IMAGE_DIR = (\n    DATA_ROOT / \"test\" / \"test_images\"\n)\n\nANNOTATION_PATH = (\n    TRAIN_DIR\n    / \"MAGFiLO_1.0_Annotations_kaggle2026_train.json\"\n)\n\nprint(f\"Dataset root: {DATA_ROOT}\")\nprint(f\"Annotation JSON: {ANNOTATION_PATH}\")\nprint(f\"YOLO model: {YOLO_MODEL_NAME}\")\nprint(f\"Image size: {IMAGE_SIZE}\")\nprint(f\"Global training batch: {BATCH_SIZE} ({YOLO_WORKERS_PER_GPU} workers per GPU)\")\nprint(\n    f\"Validation fraction: \"\n    f\"{VALIDATION_FRACTION:.0%}\"\n)\nprint(\n    f\"PQ matching IoU threshold: \"\n    f\"{PQ_MATCH_IOU:.2f}\"\n)","metadata":{"_uuid":"93dc6789-ee1a-4386-a96e-e93c1a99e76a","_cell_guid":"ebc24ac7-62b0-48b9-8120-9777c6ac3351","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-02T15:08:05.903881Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-02T15:08:05.904313Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-02T15:08:06.095456Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-02T15:08:05.904282Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-02T15:08:06.094738Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Dataset root: /kaggle/input/competitions/filament-segmentation-2026/MAGFiLO_1.0_Kaggle_2026\nAnnotation JSON: /kaggle/input/competitions/filament-segmentation-2026/MAGFiLO_1.0_Kaggle_2026/train/MAGFiLO_1.0_Annotations_kaggle2026_train.json\nYOLO model: yolo26s-seg.pt\nImage size: 2048\nGlobal training batch: 2 (2 workers per GPU)\nValidation fraction: 20%\nPQ matching IoU threshold: 0.50\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Load annotations and create a leakage-safe split\n\nThe split is performed using the physical filename rather than the COCO record ID. Multiple annotation records for the same JPEG remain on one side of the split.","metadata":{"_uuid":"e162a482-4e90-495b-ab7c-cec855bc32eb","_cell_guid":"69ee72f8-9bd7-4605-8996-d02355d6f07c","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"coco = COCO(str(ANNOTATION_PATH))\n\nimage_ids = list(coco.imgs.keys())\n\nrecords = pd.DataFrame(\n    [\n        {\n            \"image_id\": image_id,\n            \"file_name\": coco.imgs[image_id][\"file_name\"],\n        }\n        for image_id in image_ids\n    ]\n)\n\nsplitter = GroupShuffleSplit(\n    n_splits=1,\n    test_size=VALIDATION_FRACTION,\n    random_state=SEED,\n)\n\ntrain_idx, val_idx = next(\n    splitter.split(\n        records,\n        groups=records[\"file_name\"],\n    )\n)\n\ntrain_records = (\n    records\n    .iloc[train_idx]\n    .reset_index(drop=True)\n)\n\nval_records = (\n    records\n    .iloc[val_idx]\n    .reset_index(drop=True)\n)\n\ntrain_files = set(\n    train_records[\"file_name\"]\n)\n\nval_files = set(\n    val_records[\"file_name\"]\n)\n\nassert train_files.isdisjoint(\n    val_files\n), \"A physical image appears in both splits.\"\n\nprint(\n    f\"Training records: \"\n    f\"{len(train_records):,} \"\n    f\"across {len(train_files):,} physical images\"\n)\n\nprint(\n    f\"Validation records: \"\n    f\"{len(val_records):,} \"\n    f\"across {len(val_files):,} physical images\"\n)\n\nprint(\n    f\"Train/validation filename overlap: \"\n    f\"{len(train_files & val_files)}\"\n)","metadata":{"_uuid":"de763705-41e7-4445-8544-ab078a1d3b75","_cell_guid":"30aad12b-9f7e-4fe3-81dd-43b837feb889","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-02T15:08:10.219911Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-02T15:08:10.220184Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-02T15:08:12.02114Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-02T15:08:10.220158Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-02T15:08:12.020449Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"loading annotations into memory...\nDone (t=1.78s)\ncreating index...\nindex created!\nTraining records: 922 across 565 physical images\nValidation records: 232 across 142 physical images\nTrain/validation filename overlap: 0\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":6},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Build the YOLO segmentation dataset\n\nCOCO masks are converted to YOLO polygons. Input JPEGs are linked into the working dataset when possible, avoiding a second copy; a conservative copy-size estimate is included in the disk preflight.","metadata":{"_uuid":"2a9ed30a-26b3-4fbf-a6b1-6693738c516f","_cell_guid":"6c99f942-5bf3-40c0-9ca6-03fbbf39b3ec","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false}}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def configure_worker_process():\n    cv2.setNumThreads(WORKER_CPU_THREADS)\n\n    try:\n        torch.set_num_threads(\n            WORKER_CPU_THREADS\n        )\n    except RuntimeError:\n        pass\n\n    try:\n        torch.set_num_interop_threads(\n            WORKER_CPU_THREADS\n        )\n    except RuntimeError:\n        pass\n\n    try:\n        threadpool_limits(\n            limits=WORKER_CPU_THREADS\n        )\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    if hasattr(os, \"sched_getaffinity\"):\n        available_cpus = sorted(\n            os.sched_getaffinity(0)\n        )\n\n        if available_cpus:\n            identity = (\n                multiprocessing.current_process()\n                ._identity\n            )\n\n            worker_index = (\n                identity[0] - 1\n                if identity\n                else 0\n            )\n\n            cpu = available_cpus[\n                worker_index\n                % len(available_cpus)\n            ]\n\n            if hasattr(os, \"sched_setaffinity\"):\n                os.sched_setaffinity(\n                    0,\n                    {cpu},\n                )\n\n\ndef mask_to_yolo_segments(\n    mask,\n    min_area,\n):\n    mask = (mask > 0).astype(np.uint8)\n    height, width = mask.shape\n\n    count, labels, stats, _ = cv2.connectedComponentsWithStats(\n        mask,\n        connectivity=8,\n    )\n\n    segments = []\n\n    for label in range(1, count):\n        area = int(stats[label, cv2.CC_STAT_AREA])\n        if area < min_area:\n            continue\n\n        component = (labels == label).astype(np.uint8)\n\n        # FIX 1: Use CHAIN_APPROX_NONE to keep all edge pixels for the filament\n        contours, _ = cv2.findContours(\n            component,\n            cv2.RETR_EXTERNAL,\n            cv2.CHAIN_APPROX_NONE, \n        )\n\n        if not contours:\n            continue\n\n        contour = max(contours, key=cv2.contourArea)\n\n        if len(contour) < 3 or cv2.contourArea(contour) <= 0:\n            continue\n\n        points = contour.reshape(-1, 2).astype(np.float32)\n        points[:, 0] /= width\n        points[:, 1] /= height\n        points = np.clip(points, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n        if len(points) >= 3:\n            segments.append(points)\n\n    return segments\n\n\ndef worker_process_record(\n    row_dict,\n    annotation_path_str,\n    min_area,\n    train_image_dir_str,\n    image_dir_str,\n    label_dir_str,\n):\n    global _local_coco\n\n    configure_worker_process()\n\n    if \"_local_coco\" not in globals():\n        import sys\n\n        old_stdout = sys.stdout\n        sys.stdout = open(\n            os.devnull,\n            \"w\",\n        )\n\n        _local_coco = COCO(\n            annotation_path_str\n        )\n\n        sys.stdout = old_stdout\n\n    train_img_dir = Path(\n        train_image_dir_str\n    )\n\n    img_out_dir = Path(\n        image_dir_str\n    )\n\n    lbl_out_dir = Path(\n        label_dir_str\n    )\n\n    image_id = row_dict[\n        \"image_id\"\n    ]\n\n    file_name = row_dict[\n        \"file_name\"\n    ]\n\n    source_path = (\n        train_img_dir\n        / file_name\n    )\n\n    if not source_path.is_file():\n        return 0\n\n    source_suffix = source_path.suffix # Get original extension (.png, .jpg, etc)\n    source_stem = Path(file_name).stem\n    sample_stem = f\"{image_id}_{source_stem}\"\n\n    source_stem = Path(\n        file_name\n    ).stem\n\n    sample_stem = (\n        f\"{image_id}_{source_stem}\"\n    )\n\n    image_path = img_out_dir / f\"{sample_stem}{source_suffix}\"\n    label_path = lbl_out_dir / f\"{sample_stem}.txt\"\n\n    image_path.parent.mkdir(\n        parents=True,\n        exist_ok=True,\n    )\n\n    if (\n        image_path.exists()\n        or image_path.is_symlink()\n    ):\n        image_path.unlink()\n\n    try:\n        image_path.symlink_to(\n            source_path.resolve()\n        )\n    except OSError:\n        shutil.copy2(\n            source_path,\n            image_path,\n        )\n\n    annotations = (\n        _local_coco.loadAnns(\n            _local_coco.getAnnIds(\n                imgIds=[image_id]\n            )\n        )\n    )\n\n    lines = []\n\n    for annotation in annotations:\n        mask = (\n            _local_coco\n            .annToMask(annotation)\n            .astype(np.uint8)\n        )\n\n        for points in mask_to_yolo_segments(\n            mask,\n            min_area,\n        ):\n            flat = points.reshape(-1)\n\n            values = [\"0\"]\n\n            values.extend(\n                f\"{value:.6f}\"\n                for value in flat\n            )\n\n            lines.append(\n                \" \".join(values)\n            )\n\n    label_path.write_text(\n        \"\\n\".join(lines)\n        + (\"\\n\" if lines else \"\"),\n        encoding=\"utf-8\",\n    )\n\n    return len(lines)\n\n\ndef write_yolo_split_parallel(\n    split_records,\n    split_name,\n):\n    print(\n        f\"\\n[START] Building \"\n        f\"YOLO split: '{split_name}'\",\n        flush=True,\n    )\n\n    image_dir = (\n        YOLO_DATA_DIR\n        / \"images\"\n        / split_name\n    )\n\n    label_dir = (\n        YOLO_DATA_DIR\n        / \"labels\"\n        / split_name\n    )\n\n    image_dir.mkdir(\n        parents=True,\n        exist_ok=True,\n    )\n\n    label_dir.mkdir(\n        parents=True,\n        exist_ok=True,\n    )\n\n    records_list = (\n        split_records[\n            [\"image_id\", \"file_name\"]\n        ]\n        .to_dict(\n            orient=\"records\"\n        )\n    )\n\n    worker_task = partial(\n        worker_process_record,\n        annotation_path_str=str(\n            ANNOTATION_PATH\n        ),\n        min_area=MIN_COMPONENT_AREA,\n        train_image_dir_str=str(\n            TRAIN_IMAGE_DIR\n        ),\n        image_dir_str=str(\n            image_dir\n        ),\n        label_dir_str=str(\n            label_dir\n        ),\n    )\n\n    empty_labels = 0\n    total_instances = 0\n\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(\n        processes=NUM_WORKERS,\n        initializer=configure_worker_process,\n    ) as pool:\n\n        results = tqdm(\n            pool.imap_unordered(\n                worker_task,\n                records_list,\n                chunksize=4,\n            ),\n            total=len(records_list),\n            desc=(\n                f\"Preparing \"\n                f\"YOLO {split_name}\"\n            ),\n        )\n\n        for idx, instance_count in enumerate(\n            results,\n            start=1,\n        ):\n            total_instances += (\n                instance_count\n            )\n\n            if instance_count == 0:\n                empty_labels += 1\n\n            if (\n                idx == 1\n                or idx % 100 == 0\n                or idx == len(records_list)\n            ):\n                print(\n                    f\"[{split_name.upper()} Pre-Processing] \"\n                    f\"{idx:,}/\"\n                    f\"{len(records_list):,} \"\n                    f\"| polygons: \"\n                    f\"{total_instances:,} \"\n                    f\"| empty: \"\n                    f\"{empty_labels:,}\",\n                    flush=True,\n                )\n\n    print(\n        f\"[FINISHED] {split_name}: \"\n        f\"{len(records_list):,} records | \"\n        f\"{total_instances:,} polygons | \"\n        f\"empty labels: \"\n        f\"{empty_labels:,}\\n\",\n        flush=True,\n    )\n\n\nif (\n    REBUILD_YOLO_DATASET\n    and YOLO_DATA_DIR.exists()\n):\n    print(\n        f\"[CLEANUP] Removing old directory: \"\n        f\"{YOLO_DATA_DIR}\",\n        flush=True,\n    )\n\n    shutil.rmtree(\n        YOLO_DATA_DIR\n    )\n\npreflight_training_resources(\n    train_records,\n    val_records,\n    TRAIN_IMAGE_DIR,\n)\n\nwrite_yolo_split_parallel(\n    train_records,\n    \"train\",\n)\n\nwrite_yolo_split_parallel(\n    val_records,\n    \"val\",\n)\n\nDATA_YAML.write_text(\n    (\n        f\"path: \"\n        f\"'{YOLO_DATA_DIR.as_posix()}'\\n\"\n        \"train: images/train\\n\"\n        \"val: images/val\\n\"\n        \"names:\\n\"\n        \"  0: filament\\n\"\n    ),\n    encoding=\"utf-8\",\n)\n\nprint(\n    f\"YOLO dataset configuration: \"\n    f\"{DATA_YAML}\"\n)\n\nprint(\n    DATA_YAML.read_text()\n)","metadata":{"_uuid":"193f8c53-f15f-4201-8e86-a8a1ab31a965","_cell_guid":"fb5ba5ef-0d4c-4570-bdae-b6d0d94f07f6","trusted":true,"collapsed":false,"jupyter":{"outputs_hidden":false},"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-02T15:08:21.514865Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-02T15:08:21.515606Z","execution_failed":"2026-10-02T15:09:53.371Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"[CLEANUP] Removing old directory: /kaggle/working/yolo_filament_dataset\n[RAM] Available before dataset preparation: 27.1 GiB\n[DISK] Cache mode: False; estimated cache: 0.0 GiB; worst-case image copies: 0.85 GiB.\n[DISK] Planned additional use: 12.8 GiB; reserved free space: 10.0 GiB; filesystem free: 19.5 GiB.\n[DISK] Full-resolution training will continue without image caching; RAM caching is disabled.\n\n[START] Building YOLO split: 'train'\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Preparing YOLO train:   0%|          | 0/922 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"90442b24aa184b10aaf0a78bb7754c34"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stderr","text":"Exception ignored on calling ctypes callback function: <function ThreadpoolController._find_libraries_with_dl_iterate_phdr.<locals>.match_library_callback at 0x7cc9046e0400>\nTraceback (most recent call last):\nException ignored on calling ctypes callback function: Exception ignored on calling ctypes callback function  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/threadpoolctl.py\", line 1005, in match_library_callback\n<function ThreadpoolController._find_libraries_with_dl_iterate_phdr.<locals>.match_library_callback at 0x7ccaaf30bba0>    : Exception ignored on calling ctypes callback function<function ThreadpoolController._find_libraries_with_dl_iterate_phdr.<locals>.match_library_callback at 0x7cc9046e0400>\n\n: \nTraceback (most recent call last):\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/threadpoolctl.py\", line 1187, in _make_controller_from_path\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/threadpoolctl.py\", line 1005, in match_library_callback\n        <function ThreadpoolController._find_libraries_with_dl_iterate_phdr.<locals>.match_library_callback at 0x7cc9046e0400>  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/threadpoolctl.py\", line 1005, in match_library_callback\ntry:\n\n    \nTraceback (most recent call last):\n\n   File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/threadpoolctl.py\", line 1187, in _make_controller_from_path\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packa